  "fitted_prototype": "The fifth Bernoulli head reads the 84 grayscale/difference features already computed by the unmodified camera encoder diagnostics. It has independent frozen weights and RNG. The generated isolated native executable takes the physical C action. The production 4-action actor and service keep their original layouts.",
  "future_abi": "For a joint title-specific policy, version the existing SHA handshake (e.g. negotiate action count, per-head widths, critic separately). The legacy 4-head binary response is 9+2+2+2 action logits plus one value, 16 little-endian float32. TH13 needs 9+2+2+2+2 action logits and one separate value, 18 float32. Using the optional fifth TorchScript output as a C head without negotiation would confuse it with the legacy critic.",
  "future_dataset": "Store title and legal action mask. Add native X11 C to TH13 only. Package action/logp[T,5], per-step joint logp and value, request vs consumed mask, native gauge and activation as labeled telemetry. Other titles mask the extra head out of action generation, entropy, KL, advantage-ratio sum and all SFT losses. Original 4-head archives explicitly advertise 4 heads. Existing TH13 four-head inputs and returns remain usable under their original contract.",
